SUMMARY:Coffee & Crossing: Washington's Winter of 1776
DESCRIPTION:Grab a piping-hot mug of authentic colonial coffee and step rig
 ht into the high-stakes winter of 1776! Join living historian Samuel Leame
 r to uncover the bold strategy\, hidden Lancaster County connections\, and
  dramatic reality behind Washington’s famous crossing of the Delaware an
 d the epic 1st Battle of Trenton. Separate fact from fiction\, sip histori
 cal brews\, and discover how coffee and courage helped turn the tide of th
 e Revolutionary War! Registration is encouraged A Berks County native and 
 Cairn University history graduate\, Sam Leamer has spent a lifetime bringi
 ng the past to life through reenactments-- and a decade mastering the art 
 of modern coffee. By blending historical scholarship with coffee expertise
 \, Sam offers a richer\, deeper look into Colonial Coffee Culture\, showin
 g how the humble coffee bean helped fuel America’s fight for independenc
